IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-nouns`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- sections 1 and 2: short title and interpretation.
--
-- How to read a result (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING"): JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers
-- the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts.  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- Section 1 (short title) is machinery and has no rule.  Section 2 is the Act's own definitions: "court",
-- "executor" and "will".  The lead-in "unless the context otherwise requires" is a plain yes/no input on each:
-- when it is TRUE the definition is displaced and the answer is NOTHING.

§ `Section 2 -- interpretation`

-- src:89 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:90 | “court” means the General Division of the High Court;
@ref s 2 "court" (src:89-90)
GIVEN `the body is the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the body is the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the body is the General Division of the High Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“court” means the General Division of the High Court"

-- src:89 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:91 | “executor” means the executor or administrator of a deceased
-- src:92 | person, and includes, as regards any obligation, any person
-- src:93 | who takes possession of or intermeddles with the property of
-- src:94 | a deceased person;
@ref s 2 "executor" (src:89-94)
GIVEN `the person is the executor or administrator of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is about an obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes possession of or intermeddles with the property of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the person is an executor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the person is the executor or administrator of a deceased person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person takes possession of or intermeddles with the property of a deceased person` AND `the question is about an obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person takes possession of or intermeddles with the property of a deceased person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards any obligation" -- fork F-S2: an intermeddler is an executor "as regards any obligation"; asked about a right the definition neither includes nor excludes the intermeddler, so NOTHING (the other reading is JUST FALSE: "includes, as regards any obligation" read as the only inclusion)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“executor” means the executor or administrator of a deceased person"

-- src:89 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:95 | “will” includes a codicil.
@ref s 2 "will" (src:89-95)
GIVEN `the document is a codicil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the document is within the word will` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context otherwise requires` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
        IF `the document is a codicil` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“will” includes a codicil"

§§ `Section 2 -- tests`

-- Expected values are hand-written from the words of s 2, beside each assertion.
-- "court" means the General Division of the High Court
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is the court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the General Division is the court
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is the court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- any other body: "means"
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is the court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the context otherwise requires
-- "executor" means the executor or administrator ... and includes, as regards any obligation, any person who ...
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an executor or administrator
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an executor` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an intermeddler, as regards an obligation
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an executor` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an intermeddler, not as regards an obligation
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an executor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither: "means"
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an executor` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the context otherwise requires
-- "will" includes a codicil
#ASSERT `s 2 the document is within the word will` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a codicil
#ASSERT `s 2 the document is within the word will` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "includes" does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 2 the document is within the word will` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the context otherwise requires
